      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Even one glass of wine with Ambien is risky because alcohol potentiates the sedative effects of the drug, making it unpredictable. You could experience extreme drowsiness, impaired coordination, or even difficulty breathing, even if you feel it's a \"small\" amount. For your safety, it is best to stick strictly to the prescribed dosage of Ambien without any alcohol. If you are having trouble falling asleep, consider trying a non-alcoholic relaxation aid instead.",
